- **Active project:** codescout at `/home/marius/work/claude/codescout`
- (status trimmed: custom instructions)

Read a file. Large output → @file_* buffer. Markdown: heading map by default; heading=/headings= for a section, force=true for raw lines. Format-aware: json_path (JSON), toml_key (TOML/YAML). Source: a line range overlapping a symbol redirects to symbols(include_body=true); force=true bypasses.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codescout__read_file(args: {
  // Last line (1-indexed, inclusive). Needs start_line.
  end_line?: number;
  // Skip source-symbol hint and read the raw line range. Line ranges only — an oversized whole-file read is summarised either way.
  force?: boolean;
  // Markdown only: return one section by heading (e.g. "## Auth").
  heading?: string;
  // Markdown only: return several sections. Mutually exclusive with heading.
  headings?: Array<string>;
  // JSON subtree by path (e.g. "$.dependencies").
  json_path?: string;
  // Native-Read-style alias: line count from offset (end_line = offset + limit - 1). offset defaults to line 1 if omitted.
  limit?: number;
  // Native-Read-style alias: 1-indexed start line (= start_line). Ignored when start_line/end_line are set.
  offset?: number;
  // File path relative to project root
  path?: string;
  // First line (1-indexed). Without end_line: a 50-line window.
  start_line?: number;
  // TOML table or YAML section by key (e.g. "dependencies").
  toml_key?: string;
  // Absolute workspace path to resolve this call against; omit for the active project. For concurrent subagents in different workspaces.
  workspace?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

